ScoreMaker ChangeLog
====================

2026-08-05
----------

Summary: Added position-aware playback and introduced semantic voices and
explicit measures without breaking MusicKit-style .score files.

* Started playback at the selected note's tick, with beginning-of-score
  playback retained when no note is selected.
* Kept playback audio, highlighting, scrolling, pause, resume, tempo changes,
  and MIDI-output changes synchronized when playback starts after tick zero.
* Added independent voice numbers to notes; notes from legacy sources default
  to voice 1.
* Added explicit measure objects containing measure number, starting tick,
  duration, time signature, and pickup/implicit status.
* Derived conventional measures for legacy .score and MIDI files that do not
  contain explicit measure structure.
* Updated score editing and playback-copy paths to retain note voice and
  measure associations.
* Rendered barlines from explicit measure boundaries and prevented notes in
  different voices from being combined into the same beam group.
* Imported and exported MusicXML voice assignments, explicit measures, pickup
  measures, and per-measure time signatures.
* Preserved existing .score statements and V1 metadata while adding an
  ignorable, Base64-encoded JSON `ScoreMaker Structure V2` comment for voices
  and measures.
* Added `make test` compatibility coverage for every bundled .score example,
  legacy defaults, V1/V2 metadata, multi-voice scores, pickup measures, and
  .score/MusicXML round trips.
* Documented the voice, measure, and .score compatibility behavior.
* Added a resizable bottom playback monitor with an 88-key piano that
  highlights every currently sounding pitch.
* Added live per-voice MIDI-velocity meters and numeric velocity readings.
* Added stronger dark separators between adjacent white piano keys.
* Made the on-screen piano keys clickable for score entry using the current
  inspector duration, start position, and selected part.
* Added immediate audio audition when an on-screen piano key is pressed, using
  the selected part's instrument and current rhythmic duration without
  disturbing the main playback controls.
* Made the inspector vertically scrollable, increased the initial window
  height, and reserved separate non-overlapping areas for the palette and
  score-notes editor at every supported window size.
* Reset all piano-key input and playback highlights when playback stops or
  reaches the end of the score.
* Marked middle C on the on-screen piano with a `C` label.
* Made a clicked piano key remain highlighted only for its audition duration,
  then automatically reset the keyboard state and audition player.
* Fixed virtual-piano black-key entry so sharp note names and accidentals are
  retained and rendered correctly instead of being overwritten as naturals.
* Widened the initial document window and inspector so controls, palette items,
  and score notes are not clipped by the inspector scrollbar.
* Preserved imported MIDI note velocity in the score model, playback export,
  and backward-compatible V2 .score metadata; legacy notes retain the previous
  default velocity of 64.

2026-08-01
----------

Summary: Improved score completion and expanded the example library.

* Added a final double barline at the end of the composition.
* Added further example scores for exercising parsing, rendering, and
  playback.

2026-07-29
----------

Summary: Expanded MIDI and scorefile support, enriched sample music, and
corrected printing and notation behavior.

* Added MIDI-related model, parser, and playback improvements.
* Expanded document metadata handling across the parser, model, and view.
* Improved score rendering and added more example music.
* Added and corrected the Bach violin fugue example.
* Fixed scorefile parsing problems and broadened support for score grammar
  constructs.
* Corrected multi-page printing logic.

2026-07-28
----------

Summary: Moved playback to AVFoundation and stabilized the document changes.

* Updated ScoreMaker documents to use AVFoundation for MIDI playback.
* Resolved integration conflicts and applied follow-up document fixes.

2026-07-27
----------

Summary: Added expressive notation and MusicXML interoperability, then fixed
the associated parser and display issues.

* Added slurs and sharp/flat notation with related minor fixes.
* Added MusicXML import and export support.
* Corrected MusicXML document handling and parser behavior.
* Fixed delegate and score-view integration issues.
* Added editable score-title support.
* Resolved changes merged from the main branch.

2026-07-26
----------

Summary: Made playback visually track the score and substantially improved
interactive note, part, and instrument editing.

* Added live note highlighting during playback.
* Corrected drag-and-drop note positioning and snapping.
* Reflected the selected note in the inspector.
* Improved note placement and added part and instrument management.
* Added example scores and corrected document behavior.
* Applied several playback fixes and follow-up stabilization attempts.
* Integrated concurrent changes from the main branch.

2026-07-21
----------

Summary: Expanded rhythmic notation and note-entry tools.

* Added editable note durations.
* Added whole-note and half-note rendering.
* Enhanced the notation palette for entering notes of different values.

2026-07-14
----------

Summary: Added direct playback stopping.

* Added a Stop button and its playback-control behavior.

2026-07-13
----------

Summary: Stabilized playback and document shutdown.

* Fixed playback behavior.
* Stopped and deallocated MIDI-player and NSSound resources when closing a
  document.
* Updated the application icon.

2026-06-10
----------

Summary: Improved instrument consistency during playback.

* Forced playback to use SoundFont instruments where appropriate.

2026-06-05
----------

Summary: Expanded build documentation.

* Added GNUstep setup and usage instructions to the README.

2026-06-04
----------

Summary: Converted the initial viewer into a document-oriented, cross-platform
AppKit/GNUstep application with notation resources and editing foundations.

* Added and refined treble and bass clefs, supporting image resources, and
  application/document icons.
* Made the Objective-C code non-ARC, Objective-C 1.0 compatible, and usable
  with GNUstep.
* Added the document class and document-oriented creation/opening behavior.
* Added GNUstep application, menu, and recent-document fixes.
* Added new supporting classes and reorganized build inputs.
* Updated Makefile, GNUmakefile, plist, resource, and ignore configuration.
* Fixed document and score-view crashes and other initial regressions.
* Added beaming plus sharp and flat rendering.
* Corrected the README launch command and added screenshots.
* Cleaned up initial implementation issues and integrated main-branch changes.

2026-06-03
----------

Summary: Established the ScoreMaker project, licensing, layout, and first
notation capabilities.

* Added the initial application sources and project files.
* Removed generated build products and added ignore rules.
* Renamed and reorganized source directories.
* Added the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1.
* Fixed an early regression.
* Added General MIDI instrument names.
* Added initial treble- and bass-clef support.
